      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fine, though in the future you may end up wanting \"unresolved runs\" so that if multiple code points in a row are unresolved then the user also knows that a whole run was unresolved and also so the user knows where that run was in context so they could maybe re-shape even more or have more information when doing font resolution. It might also be somewhat helpful in the future to return with those runs the resolved language/script (so that the right fonts might be picked for Han unified code points).\n\nIn other words, this is a fine first step, but for a more robust solution in the future you\u0027re going to want to return a list of unresolved code point ranges, each annotated with the corresponding script and language.",
      "revId": "787af31b18ff9ba2e3627758c95accdd390776eb",
